    {
      "ordinal": 31,
      "depth": 0,
      "kind": "section",
      "number": "5",
      "title": "Rules of Tournament",
      "body": "1. Pools Scheduling a. If you have 2/3 Pools, you should alternate between the 2/3 pools in order to have reduction in breaks and delays b. If you have 4 or more pools, you should split the each set of 2 pools into separate segments throughout the day to reduce time in armor and have reasonable breaks In example: Pool A and B alternate in morning, Pool C and D alternate in afternoon c. If a team/competitor has to fight one match immediately after another, they may have up to a 5 minute break\n\n2. Round Robin Scheduling a. If a team/competitor has to fight one match immediately after another, they may have up to a 5 minute break b. If a team or competitor Drops from competing in a match they automatically lose all additional matches and are no longer allowed to continue competing in the tournament. (potential review from judiciary committee) 3. Elimination Stage a. If a team/competitor has to fight one match immediately after another, they may have up to a 5 minute break b. If a team or competitor Drops from competing in a match they automatically lose all additional matches and are no longer allowed to continue competing in the tournament. (potential review from judiciary committee) i. If this directly affects the finals, you will advance the next in place team/competitor to ensure competition for the medaling categories",
      "page_from": 8,
      "page_to": 8,
