    {
      "ordinal": 32,
      "depth": 0,
      "kind": "section",
      "number": "6",
      "title": "Definitions",
      "body": "1. Pools- Teams/competitors are divided into groups, where they all compete against each other, to determine which teams/competitors advance to the Elimination stage 2. Elimination Stage- also known as brackets/champions/knockout rounds. Stage of the tournament where participants are eliminated from the tournament after a\n\nsingle loss. The winners of each round advance to the next stage until only one competitor remains 3. Round Robin- the entire tournament is all in one group, where every team/competitor compete against each other 4. Tournament- a category that competitors compete in 5. Event- a tournament or multiple tournaments that happen in one location in a continuous series",
